ToolTree proves that **Greedy Execution** (LLM acts immediately) and **Open-Loop Planning** (LLM plans without feedback) are mathematically suboptimal. Optimal performance requires both **Pre-Execution Evaluation ($r_{pre}$)** (assessing potential) and **Post-Execution Evaluation ($r_{post}$)** (assessing result).

Our **OpenClaw** architecture maps 1:1:
- $r_{pre}$ = AGENTS.md + SKILL.md (Static Roles)
- $r_{post}$ = `read_by` + SIGNALS.md (Dynamic Validation)
- $\tau_{pre}$ = L1 PASS Criteria
- $\tau_{post}$ = Circuit Breakers

